## 16. Lessons Learned

### Design Before Code
Many problems were caught during design phase:
- One-embedding-per-document flaw
- Missing user scoping
- Chunk boundary issues

**Lesson:** Spend time on architecture. Fixing design is cheap. Fixing code is expensive.

### Security is Not Optional
Every feature had security implications. Always ask: "In a multi-user system, who owns this data?"

### Separation of Concerns Pays Off
Each service has one job. When one service needs to change (e.g., swap OpenAI for local LLM), only one file changes.

### Use Exact Specifications
When integrating external APIs, use their official libraries and exact specifications (tiktoken for OpenAI tokenization).

